#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:1
msgid "How to Extend the Framework"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:4
msgid ""
"The framework is rapidly evolving. The documentation might be out-of-sync "
"with the implementation. The purpose of this documentation is to give "
"context for upcoming reviews."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:9
msgid ""
"SSAF is designed to be extensible with new **summary extractors** and "
"**serialization formats**. Extensions can be added in three ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:12
msgid ""
"**Statically, in-tree** — built as part of the upstream LLVM/Clang tree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:13
msgid ""
"**Statically, out-of-tree (downstream)** — built in a downstream fork or "
"project that links `clangScalableStaticAnalysisCore` as a static library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:14
msgid "**Dynamically, via plugins** — loaded at runtime as shared objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:16
msgid ""
"All three approaches use the same `llvm::Registry`-based registration "
"mechanism. The key difference is how the linker sees the registration: "
"static libraries need {doc}`force-linker anchors <ForceLinkerHeaders>` to "
"prevent dead-stripping, while shared libraries do not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:20
msgid "Adding a summary extractor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:22
msgid ""
"A summary extractor is an `ASTConsumer` that inspects the AST and populates "
"a `TUSummary` via the `TUSummaryBuilder` interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:24
msgid "Step 1: Implement the extractor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:43
msgid "Step 2: Register the extractor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:61
msgid ""
"The `\"MyExtractor\"` string is the name users pass to `--ssaf-extract-"
"summaries=MyExtractor`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:63
msgid "Step 3: Add the force-linker anchor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:65
msgid ""
"See {doc}`ForceLinkerHeaders` for a full explanation of why this is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:67
msgid ""
"For **in-tree** additions, add one line to `clang/include/clang/"
"ScalableStaticAnalysis/BuiltinAnchorSources.def` (in alphabetical order):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:75
msgid ""
"`SSAFBuiltinForceLinker.h` includes this `.def` file automatically — no need "
"to edit it directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:78
msgid ""
"For **downstream** additions, see [Out-of-tree (downstream) extensions](#out-"
"of-tree-downstream-extensions) below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:80
msgid "Adding a serialization format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:82
msgid ""
"A serialization format controls how the `TUSummary` is written to (and read "
"from) disk. This involves more boilerplate than an extractor because each "
"format has a per-analysis `FormatInfo` sub-registry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:85
msgid "Step 1: Define the format class"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:87
msgid ""
"Your format class must inherit from `SerializationFormat` and define a "
"`FormatInfo` type alias:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:110
msgid "Step 2: Register the format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:130
msgid ""
"The format name (`\"myformat\"`) is matched against the file extension in `--"
"ssaf-tu-summary-file=output.myformat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:132
msgid "Step 3: Register per-analysis FormatInfo entries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:134
msgid ""
"For each analysis that should be serializable in your format, register a "
"`FormatInfo` entry. `FormatInfo` must be implemented for any of the "
"summaries that wants to support `myformat`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:154
msgid "Step 4: Add the force-linker anchor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:156
msgid ""
"Same pattern as for extractors — add the anchor to `BuiltinAnchorSources."
"def` (in alphabetical order). See [Adding a summary extractor](#adding-a-"
"summary-extractor) Step 3, and {doc}`ForceLinkerHeaders`."
msgstr ""

