msgid ""
"That's it — the `SSAFForceLinker.h` umbrella includes "
"`SSAFBuiltinForceLinker.h` transitively, so any binary that includes the "
"umbrella will pull in the registration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:171
msgid "Out-of-tree (downstream) extensions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:173
msgid ""
"Downstream projects that maintain a fork can add their own extensions "
"without modifying upstream files — reducing the risk of merge-conflicts:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:176
msgid ""
"Create a downstream force-linker header, e.g. `SSAFDownstreamForceLinker.h`, "
"containing the anchor references for downstream-only extractors and formats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:179
msgid "Include it from `SSAFForceLinker.h` (the umbrella):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:187
msgid ""
"This is a single-line addition per downstream project, minimizing conflicts "
"with upstream changes. Upstream will try to avoid modifying this umbrella "
"header, making it a stable static extension point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:190
msgid "Add the downstream source files to the build system as usual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:192
msgid "Dynamic extensibility (plugins)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:194
msgid ""
"Shared libraries loaded at runtime — via `dlopen` / `LoadLibrary` or the "
"Clang plugin mechanism — do **not** need force-linker anchors, but having "
"them also does not hurt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:197
msgid ""
"When a shared object (`.so` / `.dylib`) is loaded, the dynamic linker runs "
"all global constructors in that library unconditionally. This means the "
"`llvm::Registry::Add<>` objects execute their constructors and register "
"themselves automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:200
msgid "To use a plugin:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:202
msgid "Build your extractor or format as a shared library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:203
msgid "Load it with the Clang plugin mechanism (`-fplugin=` or `-load`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:204
msgid "Pass the extractor name to `--ssaf-extract-summaries=` as usual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ScalableStaticAnalysis/developer-docs/HowToExtend.md:206
msgid ""
"No changes to any force-linker header are required. The `llvm::Registry` "
"infrastructure handles everything once the shared object is loaded."
msgstr ""
